From b0ff49cc4fc67992639aee9ac6a39492d201e3ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 01:28:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/56] Input: aw86927 - accept the AW86937

TB323FU has two AW8693x haptic drivers on
i2c6 that report CHIPID 0x9370 (AW86937). The vendor handles the whole
AW8693x family with one driver; treat the AW86937 like the AW86938 here.
Both probe and register force-feedback input devices; playing a rumble
effect returns without error (felt by hand still to be confirmed).
---
 drivers/input/misc/aw86927.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/aw86927.c b/drivers/input/misc/aw86927.c
index f53b8f004..fa22a9bef 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/aw86927.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/aw86927.c
@@ -147,6 +147,7 @@
 #define AW86927_CHIPIDL_REG			0x58
 #define AW86927_CHIPID				0x9270
 #define AW86938_CHIPID				0x9380
+#define AW86937_CHIPID				0x9370
 
 #define AW86927_TMCFG_REG			0x5b
 #define AW86927_TMCFG_UNLOCK			0x7d
@@ -751,6 +752,7 @@ static int aw86927_detect(struct aw86927_data *haptics)
 		haptics->model = AW86927;
 		break;
 	case AW86938_CHIPID:
+	case AW86937_CHIPID:	/* same AW8693x family, handled alike by the vendor driver */
 		haptics->model = AW86938;
 		break;
 	default:
-- 
